content:
{
  "asset": "P-104 standby AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump on the filtered-water line; serial plate painted over and unreadable.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-seal condition: the seal is leaking steadily. The evidence provides no numerical allowable leakage rate or leakage-based shutdown threshold. The manual treats shaft-seal leakage as a fault requiring mechanical-seal replacement and an alignment check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: Figure 3 applies to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on the bearing housings, with the highest reading used for classification. If the reported 3.0 mm/s was measured by that method, it falls in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation'), above the Zone A boundary of 2.8 and below the Zone C restricted-operation threshold of 4.5. It is also below Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS), where damage is likely and the manual says to stop the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: the documented limits are for bearing-housing surface temperature: normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C, and trip at 90 °C. If the reported housing reading of 69 °C is a bearing-housing surface measurement, it is within the normal range: 1 °C below the normal upper limit, 11 °C below alarm, and 21 °C below trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On the documented HF-300 criteria, the reported vibration and temperature do not meet the Figure 3 stop-pump zone or the temperature alarm/trip thresholds. No evidence-based immediate-stop criterion for the steady seal leak is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces: the manual's first listed probable cause for leakage at the shaft seal; inspect the removed seal to confirm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal run dry: another listed probable cause. Investigate flush availability and any dry-running history; the HF-300 uses Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment: also listed as a probable cause of shaft-seal leakage. Check alignment against the manual tolerances during the repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before ordering or fitting the seal, establish P-104's serial number from maintenance/procurement records or another reliable identifier. For serial HF3-22000 and above, apply Service Bulletin SB-2026-014: use pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, do not fit HF3-450, and do not perform a sleeve measurement to set the cartridge. Below HF3-22000, continue with component seal HF3-450 and manual Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before beginning mechanical-seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly using lifting equipment; its documented mass is 68 kg. The HF-300 design permits removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the existing seal and shaft sleeve, and inspect the sleeve for scoring.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If SB-2026-014 applies, replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. If the pump is below HF3-22000 and scoring is found, hold the sleeve disposition for engineering/site review because the supplied manual gives an inspection instruction but no numerical scoring limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the single serial-correct replacement mechanical seal and a new HF3-120 casing gasket. The manual requires a new casing gasket with seal replacement, and the parts list requires gasket replacement whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten fasteners with lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, and any disturbed M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm. For M10 seal gland nuts, use 25 Nm only with the below-HF3-22000 HF3-450/Table 5 arrangement; use 30 Nm with HF3-450B on serial HF3-22000 and above. Do not torque the gland until serial applicability is resolved.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment as required by the seal-leakage troubleshooting procedure. Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing; acceptance tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before returning the pump to service or standby availability, confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is in service and ensure the pump is never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After repair, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3; thereafter continue the documented weekly condition-monitoring interval.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B or HF3-450 (serial-dependent; select one)",
      "description": "One mechanical seal, not both. Use pre-set cartridge HF3-450B and do not fit HF3-450 on serial HF3-22000 and above. Below HF3-22000, use component seal HF3-450. Do not release the seal for installation until P-104's serial range is established.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "New casing gasket for the seal-replacement reassembly; replace whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional shaft sleeve. Supply one if inspection shows replacement is required. For pumps covered by SB-2026-014, the documented replacement criterion is scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth; disposition for a below-HF3-22000 pump with scoring remains unresolved.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before removing the back pull-out assembly or opening the seal area.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-104 is within the P-101 to P-106 filtered-water pump group dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Confirm and apply the site's chemical isolation, PPE, draining, and decontamination controls before opening the pump; the supplied evidence identifies the chemical but does not specify those controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; manual handling without lifting equipment is not permitted by the documented specification.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement standard labour allowance: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment standard labour allowance: 1.5 hours with 1 technician when performed. Alignment checking is included in the seal-leakage corrective action, and laser alignment is mandatory after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The HF-300 manual (AQ-OM-300, Revision D) parts list and Table 5 identify component seal HF3-450 and 25 Nm seal-gland torque. AquaDyne SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, supersedes that arrangement only for HF-300 pumps with serial HF3-22000 and above: those pumps require HF3-450B and 30 Nm, while pumps below HF3-22000 continue using HF3-450 and Table 5. Decision for P-104: applicability cannot be resolved because its serial plate is unreadable. Hold seal selection, ordering for installation, and gland tightening pending serial verification; apply the bulletin at or above HF3-22000 and the manual arrangement below it. The bulletin's pre-set/no-sleeve-measurement instruction and greater-than-0.1 mm sleeve-scoring criterion must likewise not be extended to an older pump without evidence of applicability.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is P-104's actual serial number, or what reliable asset/build record establishes whether it is HF3-22000 or above? This is required to select the seal, gland torque, cartridge-setting method, and sleeve-scoring criterion.",
    "Was the 3.0 mm/s vibration reading an RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and was it the highest reading from both bearing housings as required for Figure 3 classification?",
    "Was the reported 69 °C housing temperature measured on the bearing-housing surface, to which the 70/80/90 °C limits apply?",
    "What site PPE, chemical isolation, drainage, decontamination, and leakage-response requirements apply to the sodium-hypochlorite-dosed service?",
    "If P-104 is below serial HF3-22000 and its shaft sleeve is scored, what acceptance or replacement limit should be used? The supplied manual only says to inspect for scoring.",
    "Is there any history of dry running, interruption of Plan 11 flush, or shaft misalignment that would identify the cause of the seal leakage?",
    "What additional labour, if any, should be allowed for conditional shaft-sleeve replacement or site chemical decontamination? The supplied labour table does not cover those activities."
  ]
}
